      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "QUEEN OF THINKING (8) sets the standard after a sharp second-up run at Ballina, where she was well supported and beaten a long neck over 1590m. She is still learning, but her Ballina run is clearly the strongest recent maiden form in this field, and she looks ready to take another step third-up. SARMAT (6) shapes as the main danger putting the Port Macquarie failure aside. He was checked around the home turn there after starting favourite, and his previous Lismore fourth showed he is close enough when things fall his way. ARMOURY (2) lacks a placing from nine starts, yet he has improved through the campaign and his latest fourth at this venue keeps him in the minor-money mix. MISSION STRIKE (4) resumes from Hong Kong form with two trials behind him, and his six tries around this distance for two placings give him enough profile to be competitive fresh despite the long break.",
